wels and wealth! / We do not want to receive those, O Pegan victorious in war! / Having tuned the small lute to the Sevvali melody, your hard / good country to sing, having favored me, / if you would give a gift, O Lord, you, / because of your not giving your presence, languishing and weakening, / who suffers deep grief, your wife wearing well-crafted jewels, / like the gathered base of the plumage of a proud peacock, / her abundant soft hair, having applied fragrant smoke, / to wear a cool fragrant garland, / let your horses be harnessed to the tall chariot of fast gallop!","translation":"Let your wealth and precious jewels remain as they are; we do not desire to receive them, O Pegan victorious in battle! If you, O Lord, would favor me and grant me a gift for tuning my small lute to the sevvaḻi melody and singing of your good, rugged land, then let your horses be harnessed to your tall, fast-galloping chariot, so that your wife, who wears well-crafted jewels and suffers deep grief, languishing and wasting away because of your absence, may dry her thick, soft hair—which resembles the folded feathers of a vibrant peacock—with fragrant smoke, and adorn it with a cool, sweet-smelling garland.","modern":"போரில் வெல்லும் பேகனே! உன்னுடைய அரிய அணிகலன்களும் செல்வங்களும் அப்படியே இருக்கட்டும். அவற்றை நாங்கள் பெற விரும்பவில்லை. தலைவனே! சிறிய யாழில் செவ்வழிப் பண்ணை இசைத்து, உன்னுடைய வன்புல நன்னாட்டினைப் பாடிய எனக்கு, நீ விரும்பிப் பரிசில் தர நினைத்தால், உன்னுடைய பிரிவால் வருந்தி, மெலிந்து, பெருந்துன்பம் அனுபவிக்கும் உன்னுடைய திருந்திய அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த மனைவி, செருக்குமிக்க மயிலின் தோகை சுருங்கி நிற்பது போன்ற தன் அடர்ந்த மென்மையான கூந்தலுக்கு நறுமணப் புகையூட்டி, குளிர்ந்த நறுமண மாலையைச் சூடிக் கொள்ளுமாறு, உன்னுடைய வேகமான குதிரைகள் உனது நெடிய தேரில் பூட்டப்படட்டும்! நீ அவளிடம் விரைந்து செல்வாயாக!","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Aricil Kiḻār addresses the chieftain Pegan, who has abandoned his wife Kaṇṇaki for a courtesan. The poet states that he does not desire any material wealth, gold, or precious jewels as a reward for singing of Pegan's rugged, beautiful land. Instead, the only gift he begs for is for Pegan to return immediately to his grieving wife. The poet describes the wife's thick, soft hair as resembling the folded feathers of a vibrant peacock, showing how she has neglected her appearance in her sorrow. By returning, Pegan will allow her to dry her hair with fragrant incense and wear fresh garlands once more, restoring her joy. This poem belongs to Peruntiṇai, representing unmatched love and the poet's intervention to correct the chieftain's behavior.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,0.8],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.5],[1.5,2.2],[2.2,2.5],[2.5,2.6],[2.6,3.47],[3.47,3.6],[3.6,4.7],[4.7,4.8],[4.8,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,5.7],[5.7,6.8],[6.8,6.9],[6.9,7.1],[7.1,7.4],[7.4,8.7],[8.7,8.77],[8.79,8.8],[8.8,10.0],[10.0,10.1],[10.1,11.0],[11.0,11.1],[11.27,11.44],[11.61,12.3],[12.3,13.3],[13.3,13.9],[13.9,14.6],[14.6,14.8],[14.8,15.4],[15.4,16.6],[16.6,17.35],[17.35,17.5],[18.24,18.84],[18.84,18.94],[18.94,19.64],[19.64,19.74],[20.24,20.74],[20.74,21.04],[21.04,21.24],[21.24,21.24],[21.24,23.14],[23.14,23.44],[23.44,23.54],[23.54,23.74]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.9],[0.9,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.4,2.0],[2.0,2.9],[2.9,3.2],[3.2,3.3],[3.3,4.2],[4.35,4.5],[4.5,5.9],[5.9,6.1],[6.1,6.7],[6.7,7.0],[7.0,7.4],[7.4,8.6],[8.6,8.7],[8.7,9.0],[9.0,9.4],[9.4,11.1],[11.1,11.6],[11.68,12.0],[12.0,12.5],[12.5,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.2,13.3],[13.44,13.86],[14.0,14.5],[14.5,15.5],[15.5,16.1],[16.1,16.7],[16.7,16.8],[16.8,17.1],[17.1,17.4],[17.4,17.7],[17.7,18.0],[20.8,21.4],[21.4,21.6],[21.6,22.3],[22.3,22.42],[22.8,23.5],[23.5,23.9],[23.9,24.0],[24.0,25.4],[25.4,25.9],[25.9,26.2],[26.2,26.4],[26.4,26.5]]},"sync":[[["அன்ன","like those"]],[["ஆக","let it be"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["அருங்கல","precious jewels"]],[["வெறுக்கை","wealth"]],[["அவை","those"]],[["பெறல்","receiving"]],[["வேண்டேம்","we do not want"]],[["அடுபோர்","victorious in war"],["பேக","O Pegan!"]],[["பேக","O Pegan!"]],[["சீறியாழ்","small lute"]],[["செவ்வழி","Sevvali melody"]],[["பண்ணி","having tuned"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["வன்புல","hard land"]],[["நன்னாடு","good country"]],[["பாட","to sing"]],[["என்னை","me"]],[["நயந்து","having favored"]],[["பரிசில்","gift"]],[["நல்குவை","you give"]],[["ஆயின்","if"]],[["குரிசில்","O Lord!"]],[["நீ","you"]],[["நல்காமையின்","because of not giving your presence"]],[["நல்காமையின்","because of not giving your presence"]],[["நைவர","to languish"],["சாஅய்","having weakened"]],[["சாஅய்","having weakened"]],[["அருந்துயர்","deep grief"]],[["உழக்கும்","who suffers"],["நின்","your"]],[["திருந்திழை","well-crafted jewels"]],[["அரிவை","wife"]],[["கலி","vibrant"],["மயில்","peacock's"]],[["கலாவம்","plumage"]],[["கால்","base"],["குவித்தன்ன","like gathered"]],[["குவித்தன்ன","like gathered"]],[["ஒலி","abundant"],["மென்","soft"]],[["கூந்தல்","hair"]],[["கமழ்புகை","fragrant smoke"]],[["கொளீஇ","having applied"]],[["தண்","cool"],["கமழ்","fragrant"]],[["கோதை","garland"]],[["புனைய","to wear"]],[["வண்பரி","fast-galloping"]],[["நெடுந்தேர்","tall chariot"]],[["பூண்க","let them be harnessed"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["மாவே","horses indeed"]]]}